# missingmed — Missing-data causal mediation (R package, mediationverse)
# Scope decided 2026-06-04 (Data-Wise/missingmed#1): general CRAN-targeted toolkit —
# MI + IPW estimators, SEM + GLM models, MAR + MNAR sensitivity. S7-first.
# Thin orchestration layer: fit via medfit, infer via rmediation, simulate via medsim.

## 0.5.1 (released 2026-10-07; PRs #28-#36)
- 2026-10-07 (released): v0.5.1. Bump PR #36 -> dev (b5dcb2a, squash);
  release PR #37 dev -> main (12ad874, merge commit); CI green on main;
  tag v0.5.1 on 12ad874; GitHub release "missingmed 0.5.1" (latest,
  03:44Z 2026-10-08). Gate: tests 1281 (medfit 0.4.0) / 1277 + 2 skip
  (0.3.2); check --as-cran 0/0/0. pkgdown root serves 0.5.1. r-universe
  still 0.5.0 at release time (polls main). dev stays at 0.5.1 (no .9000
  bump yet).
- 2026-10-07 (merged): PR #35 feature/docs-site -> dev (0f6e869, squash). Website audit items
  1-2: pkgdown development mode auto (site deployed dev builds at the root;
  root stays dev-built until the next main build or a manual
  workflow_dispatch on main); conf_int implemented (pool() adds per-coef
  conf_low/high on Rubin t); DESCRIPTION rewritten; inst/CITATION; S4 pages
  marked deprecated (0.6.0); paper references made generic. Tests 1281 /
  1277+2 skip; check 0/0/0. Remaining audit items: new docs 1-5 (supported-
  models article, X:M technical section, verb examples, FAQ, S4 migration).
- 2026-10-07 (merged): PR #34 feature/vignette-replication -> dev
  (29daa69, squash). New vignette worked-analysis.Rmd: tutorial of
  the paper's illustrative-analysis steps on simulated data (no manuscript
  values), Part 1 core workflow, Part 2 what dev adds over 0.5.0. Check
  --as-cran 0/0/0; renders in 1.8 s.
- 2026-10-07 (merged): PR #33 feature/review-followups -> dev (a368e85,
  squash). #32's open
  questions 1-5: pool_sem() Rubin t p-values (was geometric mean of p) + CIs;
  NA-aware tipping point; sensitivity_mnar(ariv =); warnings for args a type
  ignores; integer seed recorded. Tests 1275 pass (0.4.0) / 1271 + 2 skip
  (0.3.2); check 0/0/0; 8 new tests fail on dev (positive control).
- 2026-10-07 (merged): PR #32 feature/defensive-tests -> dev (1506c45,
  squash). Defensive
  checks + engine validation/error catching + edge-case and E2E tests across
  S7, MNAR, MBCO, IPW and S4, from five parallel units (each probed bad input
  on dev first: silent-wrong -> guard, obscure crash -> clear error, clear ->
  pin, works -> leave). Fixes: pool() stacked estimates by position;
  infer() ignored unknown ...; deprecated S4 run_sem() never worked (swapped
  args) and lav_mice() rejected valid syntax. Gate: tests 1231 pass (medfit
  0.4.0) / 1227 + 2 skip (0.3.2), check --as-cran 0/0/0, coverage 78.9 ->
  94.3%. Open questions listed in the PR body.
- 2026-10-07 (merged): PR #31 feature/set-md-validation -> dev (e49804e,
  squash; P1). Shared
  .check_roles() for set_md_mediation() and mbco_d4() (mbco_d4 tightened:
  formula_m's response may involve only the mediator; the mediator may not be
  formula_y's response); set_md_mediation()-only .check_md_spec() on
  data-expanded terms: bare X/M main effects + one X:M in formula_y, X:M needs
  gaussian identity, numeric treatment (logical refused: medfit errors on
  XTRUE). E2E: wrong-LHS control silently accepted on dev, refused now; pooled
  a/b/c_prime identical before/after. Tests 553 pass (dev baseline 503);
  check --as-cran 0/0/0 locally.
- 2026-10-07 (merged): PR #30 feature/spec-p3-engine-evidence -> dev
  (a4e38dd, squash). Grill evidence line corrected (medfit 0.4.0 accepts glm
  and regmedint; 0.3.2 glm only); P3 added to the SEM spec as a proposed,
  open amendment.
- 2026-10-07 (merged): PR #29 feature/pool-mref -> dev (bbb89b3, squash).
  Fixes a Codex adversarial-review finding on #28: averaging int_ref mixed
  each imputation's theta3 with its own m_ref. pool() now averages m_ref
  (recovered as m_star + int_ref/theta3, with a b0 + covariate-means
  fallback when theta3 = 0) and sets int_ref = theta3 * (m_ref - m_star) from
  pooled values; differing m_star across imputations errors. Read back from
  int_ref because CRAN medfit 0.3.2 (CI) lacks the covariate-means
  attribute. Gate: CI R-CMD-check + pkgdown green; local check vs medfit
  0.3.2 1 NOTE, 504 pass.
- 2026-10-07 (merged): PR #28 feature/pool-interaction -> dev (2450c71,
  squash), closes #20. pool() sets the X:M path properties in one props<-
  call, pools theta3 and recomputes the four-way decomposition (int_ref
  averaged); .pool_wald() tolerates the interaction class's missing family
  props and gives theta3/b0 their source rows' df. infer(type = "mc") gains
  treatment_level (required on X:M fits, error elsewhere; RMediation::ci() on
  pooled (a, b, theta3)); sensitivity_mnar passes it through; print/summary
  show the X:M indirect effect at x = 0 and 1. Gate: check --as-cran 1 NOTE
  (incoming baseline), tests 498 pass (was 459); known-answer MC test, planted
  wrong estimand caught (2 failures).

